content.content:
{"result":"{
  "id": "18418",
  "key": "SFCC-225",
  "summary": "PDP – Product Badges — Merchandiser Configuration",
  "description": "**As a** Site Merchandiser, \n\n**I want** to create, assign, and manage product badges (such as Runway, Campaign, Exclusive, Online Exclusive, and VIC Exclusive) without code deployment, \n\n**so that** I can keep badge content accurate and up to date across all storefronts.\n\n----\n\nThis story is the merchandiser counterpart to SFCC-132 (PDP UI – Product Badges), which builds the PWA component that renders badges on the PDP. \n\nThis story covers:\n\n- Creating and naming badge types in BM (confirmed that badges are not coming from AP21)\n- Assigning one or more badges to a product in BM\n- Configuring the priority hierarchy that determines display order when multiple badges apply, and being able to reorder this without a code change.\n      - For initial build - we can configure it as Runway (1) > Campaign (2) > Exclusive (3) but this should be configurable\n- Linking each badge to its corresponding category PLP URL\n- Supporting locale-specific badge labels (e.g. translated labels per storefront locale)\n- Region-aware badge visibility (a badge may apply on some storefronts but not others)",
  "status": {
    "name": "In QA",
    "category": "In Progress",
    "color": "yellow"
  },
  "issue_type": {
    "name": "Story"
  },
  "priority": {
    "name": "High"
  },
  "assignee": {
    "display_name": "Krizel B. Bartolome",
    "name": "Krizel B. Bartolome",
    "email": "krizel.b.bartolome@accenture.com",
    "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f08170b23c857595c1817880abba16ea?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FKB-3.png"
  },
  "reporter": {
    "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
    "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
    "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
  },
  "labels": [
    "CRM-163",
    "Custom",
    "PRD-005",
    "PRD-006",
    "Squad-A"
  ],
  "created": "2026-07-23T15:00:12.815+1000",
  "updated": "2026-09-02T19:32:53.221+1000",
  "comments": [
    {
      "id": "13577",
      "body": "User:557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8 Hey Tim, Mani and I were discussing this story on the translation requirement - in SFCC we can translate category names - but will be have Transperfect do that?",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-07-29T13:59:54.622+1000",
      "updated": "2026-07-29T13:59:54.622+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13599",
      "body": "User:5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d, yeah we should have TP do all translation of metadata configured within SFCC",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Tim Lavelle",
        "name": "Tim Lavelle",
        "email": "timothy.lavelle@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8/69afd82c-3275-4f1a-82c5-96388b537351/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-07-31T07:55:05.410+1000",
      "updated": "2026-07-31T07:55:05.410+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13658",
      "body": "Removes 2 acceptance criteria from this user story because we can’t yet test that in the BM user story - this will need to be tested in the front-end user story which is [SFCC-132](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-132) (those Acceptance criteria are already in there).\n1. Given a badge has locale-specific label translations configured, when a shopper views the PDP in a non-English locale, then the translated badge label is displayed. (will be tested as part of the UI story - SFCC-\n1. Given a product is assigned to a badge category that is configured as region-specific (e.g. AU only), when a shopper views the PDP on a different storefront (e.g. US), then the badge is not displayed.\nFYI User:712020:4ec4770e-9470-4885-9753-69a36b6cf950",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-04T12:23:06.256+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-04T12:23:06.256+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13929",
      "body": "User:5f506d223e9e2e004d7c48ac User:557058:09af9e5b-661b-42a2-90ec-9ce9f69d324d\nWe moved certain AC due to frontend to [SFCC-132](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-132) but as User:5f506d223e9e2e004d7c48ac noted this ticket still has front-end depedent AC - they will have to be tested as part of [SFCC-132](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-132).\n1. Given a Site Merchandiser creates a new badge type category in BM, when the category is saved and a product is assigned to it, then it renders on the PDP/PLP without a code deployment.\n1. Given a Site Merchandiser creates a new badge type category in BM, when the category is saved, then that category does \\*\\*not\\*\\* appear as a navigation category on the storefront.\n1. Given a Site Merchandiser updates the badge priority hierarchy in BM, when the change is saved, then the new order is reflected on the PDP without a code deployment.\n1. Given a Site Merchandiser assigns a badge, when a shopper clicks the badge on the PDP, then they are navigated to the correct badge category PLP.\n1. Given a Site Merchandiser removes a product from a badge category in BM, when the change is saved, then the badge no longer appears on the PDP/PLP.\nApologies for the confusion! Will make a note in [SFCC-132](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-132) as well.",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-20T13:56:11.521+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-20T13:56:11.521+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "14071",
      "body": "User:60084df92b411b0076ad73d6 I have raised a PR for this US.\n\nChanges:\n\n- Added  `cartridges/plugin_zim_scapi/cartridge/scripts/hooks/shop/productModifyGETResponse.js` — new product SCAPI hook: resolves the badge categories from the master product, sorts by `badgePriorityOrder` from site preference, writes {{c_productBadges: { productBadge, productBadgeUrl }, { productBadge, productBadgeUrl }, ..}} to the product response\n- added two String site preferences to a new `Badges` attribute group on `SitePreferences`:\n      - `badgePriorityOrder` — comma-delimited badge category ID display order\n      - `badgeRootCategoryId` — root category ID whose direct children are badge categories (defaults to `badges` in code if unset)\n\n[https://github.com/ZimmermannAU/zimmermann-sfcc/pull/28](https://github.com/ZimmermannAU/zimmermann-sfcc/pull/28|smart-card)\n\ncc User:557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8 User:5f506d223e9e2e004d7c48ac User:5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Victor T. Crisostomo",
        "name": "Victor T. Crisostomo",
        "email": "victor.t.crisostomo@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:09af9e5b-661b-42a2-90ec-9ce9f69d324d/0ead87b0-7d31-4296-b27b-4a7b26ac2af1/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-27T19:46:41.568+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-27T19:46:41.568+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "14168",
      "body": "This has been approved and merged",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Gideon R. Linsangan",
        "name": "Gideon R. Linsangan",
        "email": "gideon.r.linsangan@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e4458ee16511f43322ad20e3d46ffe2a?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FGL-6.png"
      },
      "created": "2026-09-01T13:42:26.327+1000",
      "updated": "2026-09-01T13:42:26.327+1000"
    }
  ]
}"}

