{
  "id": "18418",
  "key": "SFCC-225",
  "summary": "PDP – Product Badges — Merchandiser Configuration",
  "description": "**As a** Site Merchandiser, \n\n**I want** to create, assign, and manage product badges (such as Runway, Campaign, Exclusive, Online Exclusive, and VIC Exclusive) without code deployment, \n\n**so that** I can keep badge content accurate and up to date across all storefronts.\n\n----\n\nThis story is the merchandiser counterpart to SFCC-132 (PDP UI – Product Badges), which builds the PWA component that renders badges on the PDP. \n\nThis story covers:\n\n- Creating and naming badge types in BM (confirmed that badges are not coming from AP21)\n- Assigning one or more badges to a product in BM\n- Configuring the priority hierarchy that determines display order when multiple badges apply, and being able to reorder this without a code change.\n      - For initial build - we can configure it as Runway (1) > Campaign (2) > Exclusive (3) but this should be configurable\n- Linking each badge to its corresponding category PLP URL\n- Supporting locale-specific badge labels (e.g. translated labels per storefront locale)\n- Region-aware badge visibility (a badge may apply on some storefronts but not others)",
