{"result":"{
  "id": "18828",
  "key": "SFCC-464",
  "summary": "Sale Price Display — Original & Sale Price UI Across All Surfaces",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper, \n**I want** to see both the original RRP and the active sale price when a product is on sale, \n**so that** I can clearly understand the discount I am receiving.\n\nPer PRC-09, when a sale pricebook entry is active in SFCC, the PWA must render a **\"Was / Now\"** price treatment across: PLP product tiles, PDP, cart, checkout, wishlist, recommended product tiles, and order history.\n\nCross-epic dependency: PLP, PDP, Cart, Order History epics.\n\n\n**Design pattern:**\n\n  - **\"Was RRP\"* — displayed in muted/grey styling. Always the base RRP pricebook price, regardless of any previous sale price.\n  - **\"Now sale price\"* — displayed in prominent green styling. Always the most recent active sale pricebook price.\n\n\"Was\" is always the base RRP — it does not reflect a previous promotional price or a prior sale price. \"Now\" is always the currently active sale pricebook entry.\n\n\nReference Image (Figma is leading)\n\n![\"image-20260901-053421.png\"](image-20260901-053421.png)\n\n![\"image-20260901-053502.png\"](image-20260901-053502.png)",
